+# Portable exact-core correctness consumer — SOURCE ONLY
+
+This is the missing non-JVM correctness entrypoint for task598, not a timing framework. It is UNRESOLVED, UNCOMPILED and UNRUN. No dependency was downloaded, no numerical library was executed and no benchmark/build was started while task539 was running. Final published Krogu inputs must come from the accepted539 snapshot, not any current intermediate artifact. No manually asserted acceptance boolean replaces the actual task/commit/publication evidence.
+
+The existing JVM consumer remains unchanged in `../prepared-harness`: two peers (IonsPin0.3.10 and KBigNum0.0.20), Krogu, public JDK oracle and the reviewed larger fixture set. This separate Kotlin2.4.21 consumer reuses ONLY its reviewed Contract.kt, KroguAdapter.kt and IonsPinAdapter.kt. It neither includes JVM fixtures nor duplicates/reads a peer implementation. The three platform actuals report their target/runtime; Node targets fail before peer operations unless Node is24.16.0. Native's label names the declared macOS Arm64 compilation target, not collected OS/runtime evidence.
+
+| Actual future target | Candidate common peers | Explicit unavailable cells |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Kotlin/JS on Node24.16.0, CommonJS | Krogu + published IonsPin0.3.10 JS variant | Public java.math JDK and KBigNum0.0.20 have no matching JS variant |
+| Kotlin/Wasm-JS on Node24.16.0 | Krogu + published IonsPin0.3.10 Wasm-JS variant | JDK and KBigNum0.0.20 unavailable; no Float-construction workaround |
+| Kotlin/Native macOS Arm64 | Krogu + published IonsPin0.3.10 macOS Arm64 variant | JDK unavailable; KBigNum0.0.20 iOS KLIB is not a macOS runtime variant |
+
+This does not establish current artifact compatibility or prove no other peer exists. Published coverage and source links are already in `../peer-selection-preparation.md` and `../operation-semantic-matrix.md`. Additional Linux/iOS/MinGW variants are not silently claimed as tested targets. Kt-math remains a possible second JS peer with public API signatures unresolved in that preparation; this consumer does not invent an adapter from its implementation. Two actual comparable peers are presently prepared on JVM; sparse platforms remain honest one-peer intersections until another peer is qualified.
+
+## Static oracle and invariants
+
+PortableUntimedMain.kt contains four integer and four decimal pairs: zero, signed inputs, a30-bit carry/decimal scale case and a wide power-of-ten case. Expected add/subtract/product/self-square values are immutable independent constants, not generated by either peer or copied from peer benchmark tables. The carry square follows `(2^30-1)^2 = 2^60-2^31+1`; the wide square is `(10^20)^2=10^40`. Decimal coefficients/scale examples are exact elementary decimal arithmetic (for example1.20×3.400=4.08000 and−1.25×0.05=−0.0625). The future JVM/public-JDK check must independently validate these same constants before any timed cohort is eligible; no actual oracle PASS is claimed here.
+
+Every initial parse observation is checked against the independently specified input value. Each add/subtract/multiply/self-alias call executes twice on the same objects, checking both input observations before/after each call and retained earlier result observations across varying fixtures. Separately parsed equal operands get a distinct-equal ID only if reference identities differ; interning produces an explicit NA row. Signs, zero, physically aliased self multiplication and distinct inputs are preserved. Integer observations require exact decimal strings. Decimal observations use a bounded string-only canonical coefficient/exponent comparison outside any timing: numerically equivalent formatting is allowed, internal scale/cohort is NOT inferred. No peer arithmetic is repaired or replaced by oracle code.
+
+The expected mandatory core is128 CHECK598 rows (two peers×two number families×four fixtures×four operations×two repetitions). Up to32 additional distinct-equal rows depend on actual identity behavior, and explicit interning NA rows account for omitted cases. COMPLETE598_UNTIMED_ONLY appears only after every check succeeds. Mismatches and unexpected exceptions fail execution. Unsupported targets/operations are explicitly NA, never caught and relabelled successful parity. This small portability gate complements the existing JVM corpus; it is not the complete future comparison corpus or an immutability proof.
+
+Significant HALF_EVEN, cohort-strict decimal, signed quotient/bitwise, fixed-scale peer intersections, malformed-input contracts, parse/format workloads, cache states and memory controls remain as specified by the operation matrix. No ambiguous HALF_EVEN mapping or fixed-scale substitute was added. Observed correctness objects must not be reused as cold timing inputs; the later source-bound comparison uses separately prepared same-input cohorts and the existing accepted sampling/provenance scheme.
+
+## Future isolated build/run inputs
+
+Use the root Gradle wrapper9.8.1/checksum with this independent `-p` build. Kotlin is pinned2.4.21; IonsPin0.3.10 remains benchmark-only. `kroguRepository` is a dedicated isolated local Maven repository, containing the final accepted root metadata AND JS/Wasm/macOS Arm64 published KLIBs. No producer sources, worker/test modules, friend access or copied numerical assets are used.
+
+The publication ledger schema is the already reviewed task539 consumer schema:
+
+```json
+{"sourceCommit":"40-hex accepted539 commit","group":"io.heapy.krogu","module":"krogu-math","version":"exact GAV version","files":[{"path":"relative Maven file","bytes":123,"sha256":"64-hex"}]}
+```
+
+The build checks the exact ledger SHA, commit/GAV, every member size/SHA and the complete isolated repository inventory before compilation and again after a successful run task. It rejects extra resolver-visible publication files and symbolic links in the walked tree. Exact selected peer variants, transitive resolutions/licenses, compiler/runtime inputs, emitted artifact SHA and dependency locks must still be captured/reviewed during the future authorized first resolution/compile. Metadata alone is not actual resolution proof.
+
+Node is preinstalled and SHA-bound (`nodeExecutable`, `nodeSha256`), its directory must be first in PATH, and automatic Node/JDK installation is disabled. The documented [NodeJsPlugin/NodeJsEnvSpec DSL](https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-project-setup.html#node-js) supplies version24.16.0/download=false. Both Node actuals separately check the real process version. No code in this preparation was executed to validate the Gradle DSL or task names.
+
+From repository root, run exactly ONE target task per invocation, with a fresh `runName`; replace all FINAL_* placeholders with accepted evidence. The same command applies to JS, Wasm and Native by choosing respectively `jsNodeProductionRun`, `wasmJsNodeProductionRun`, or `runReleaseExecutableMacosArm64`:
